        <briefdescription>
<para>Relaxed load of a word a lock-free reader may catch mid-write. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Compiles to a plain MOV on x86-64 and a plain LDR on ARM64 <ndash/> identical codegen to a raw read. It exists to satisfy the memory model where the word is concurrently written by <ref refid="namespaceecss_1_1Memory_1_1Sector_1a26358a3fb6eceaa40f97bcf3384d8321" kindref="member">Sector::markAlive&lt;true&gt;</ref>/markNotAlive&lt;true&gt;, and, in the single-threaded build, to stop the vectoriser from reordering the surrounding scan.</para>
<para>Parameterised on ThreadSafe alone rather than living in <ref refid="classecss_1_1Memory_1_1SectorsArray" kindref="compound">SectorsArray</ref>, so that code which needs the load without naming an allocator can share the one definition. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
